From <@U08URAB899P> :slightly_smiling_face:
&gt; *Meridian Labs is hiring for two roles!*
&gt; 
&gt; We're a nonprofit building open source infrastructure for evaluating and understanding AI models, including Inspect AI, Inspect Scout, Inspect Petri and Inspect Flow. Our tools are used by AI Security Institutes in the UK, US, EU, Japan and Korea, as well as METR, Apollo Research, Epoch AI and Redwood Research. Because so many organizations build on the same platform, improvements we make with one partner reach all of them.
&gt; Several people on our team currently hold roles at UK AISI, US CAISSI and RAND, and we collaborate closely with our government partners on platform adoption and on the tools and research that power evaluations, pre-deployment testing, transcript analysis, incident investigations, and many other projects.
&gt; 
&gt; *Member of Technical Staff, Research* ($175k–$325k): As frontier models get more capable, the tools for evaluating and monitoring them need to keep up. Investigating what models do increasingly means making sense of thousands of long agent transcripts, and the AI tools researchers rely on often miss things and overstate their confidence. Projects include improving scalable alignment evals, building open source monitors, and making large-scale transcript analysis faster and more trustworthy. What you build gets used directly by our partners in their own projects. Looking for strong Python, hands-on LLM experience, relevant research experience, and someone who likes getting into the weeds. <https://meridianlabs.ai/careers/mts-research|meridianlabs.ai/careers/mts-research>
&gt; 
&gt; *Technical Operations Manager* ($110k–$160k): Our first ops hire, working directly with our CEO. Alongside running finance, tooling and compliance (and automating as much of it as possible), you'd own the operational side of our partnerships with governments, labs and other nonprofits: agreements, security reviews, partner reporting, and joint visits and events. A great fit for someone who uses AI tools daily and loves automating repetitive work. <https://meridianlabs.ai/careers/technical-operations-manager|meridianlabs.ai/careers/technical-operations-manager>
&gt; 
&gt; Both roles are Bay Area, Boston, or London, with remote possible for the right person. More at <https://meridianlabs.ai/careers|meridianlabs.ai/careers>. To apply, email your resume and a short note on why you're interested to <mailto:jobs@meridianlabs.ai|jobs@meridianlabs.ai>. If you don't meet every qualification, we'd still love to hear from you, and please share with anyone you think might be a fit!

